3. Source Availability for Core Components

If You Distribute, or make available as a Network Service, a version
of the Software that contains modifications to any file or directory
listed in CORE-COMPONENTS.md, then You must:

  (a) make the corresponding source code of those modified Core
      Components available under this License (OIE-PCS-1.0) to all
      recipients of the Distributed Software or to all users of the
      Network Service;
  (b) clearly identify which Core Components have been modified and
      the nature of those modifications;
  (c) provide reasonable instructions for obtaining the corresponding
      source code; and
  (d) retain this License, the copyright notice, and the LICENSE-POLICY.md
      in any redistribution.

Modifications to files and directories NOT listed in CORE-COMPONENTS.md
are not subject to the source-availability obligations of this Section
when Distributed without Commercial Use, but remain subject to
Section 4 when Distributed as part of Commercial Use.

Private internal modification of Core Components that is never
Distributed and never made available as a Network Service is not
subject to the source-availability obligation of this Section.


