16. Dispute Resolution

Any dispute, controversy, or claim arising out of, relating to, or
in connection with this License, including any question regarding
its existence, validity, interpretation, performance, breach, or
termination (a "Dispute"), shall be referred to and finally
resolved by arbitration administered by the **Hong Kong
International Arbitration Centre (HKIAC)** in accordance with the
HKIAC Administered Arbitration Rules in force at the time of filing
(the "Rules"), which Rules are deemed to be incorporated by
reference into this Section 16.

  (a) **Seat (legal place) of arbitration**: Hong Kong.
  (b) **Venue (physical hearing)**: Hong Kong, unless the parties
      agree otherwise or the tribunal orders otherwise.
  (c) **Number of arbitrators**: one (1), unless the amount in
      dispute exceeds USD 1,000,000 in which case three (3).
  (d) **Language of arbitration**: English, with the right of any
      party to submit Chinese-language documentary evidence without
      translation, at the tribunal's discretion.
  (e) **Governing procedural law**: the Hong Kong Arbitration
      Ordinance (Cap. 609) and the Rules.
  (f) **Confidentiality**: the arbitration shall be confidential,
      and any award shall be confidential, except as required by
      law or for the purpose of enforcement.
  (g) **Interim relief**: nothing in this Section 16 prevents any
      party from seeking interim or injunctive relief from any
      court of competent jurisdiction to preserve the status quo or
      prevent irreparable harm (in particular, trademark
      infringement or unauthorized Commercial Use of the Brand),
      pending the constitution of the tribunal.
  (h) **Class-action waiver**: any arbitration shall be conducted
      on an individual basis only. Disputes may not be consolidated
      or arbitrated on a class, representative, or private
      attorney-general basis.
  (i) **Small-claims carve-out**: either party may bring an
      individual action in a court of competent jurisdiction for
      disputes within the scope of that court's small-claims or
      equivalent summary procedure, if available.

The arbitral award shall be final and binding on the parties and
may be enforced in any court of competent jurisdiction under, among
others, the Arrangement for Reciprocal Enforcement of Judgments in
Civil and Commercial Matters between the Mainland and Hong Kong
(2019), the New York Convention on the Recognition and Enforcement
of Foreign Arbitral Awards (1958), and the Hague Convention on the
Recognition and Enforcement of Foreign Judgments in Civil or
Commercial Matters (2019/2023).


17. Commercial License Terms — Term, Devices, Upgrades

Where a commercial license is granted under Section 4, the
following defaults apply unless the executed commercial agreement
expressly states otherwise:

  (a) **Term**: one (1) year from the Effective Date stated in the
      commercial agreement, renewable for successive one-year
      terms unless either party gives at least sixty (60) days'
      written notice of non-renewal before the end of the current
      term.

  (b) **Devices**: the number of devices, named users, regions, or
      other usage metric stated in the commercial agreement. Use
      beyond the licensed metric requires an upgrade addendum and
      pro-rated fee; continued over-deployment after written
      notice is a material breach.

  (c) **Upgrades**: during the term, the licensee is entitled to
      patches, minor releases (e.g. v2.6 → v2.7), and security
      updates at no additional charge. Major-version upgrades
      (e.g. v2.x → v3.x) are NOT automatic; the licensee may
      extend coverage to a new major version by paying an upgrade
      fee, which the Project Copyright Holder will quote on
      request. Use of a new major version without the upgrade
      addendum reverts that version to OIE-PCS-1.0.

  (d) **Beta / pre-release**: pre-release versions made available
      to the licensee are provided "AS IS" and may be subject to a
      separate pre-release agreement; they are NOT warranted.


18. Commercial License Terms — Pricing, Payment, Taxes

  (a) **Pricing model**: the indicative tiers set out in
      COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md form the starting point for
      negotiation. The actual fees are stated in the executed
      commercial agreement. The Project Copyright Holder reserves
      the right to revise pricing for new agreements and renewals
      on thirty (30) days' written notice; in-flight agreements
      are unaffected.

  (b) **Payment terms**: invoices are due net thirty (30) days
      from the invoice date unless otherwise stated. Late payment
      accrues interest at the lesser of (i) 1.5% per month
      (compounded monthly) and (ii) the maximum rate permitted by
      applicable law.

  (c) **Taxes**: all fees are exclusive of applicable taxes,
      duties, and levies (including VAT, GST, sales tax, and
      withholding tax). The licensee is responsible for any taxes
      associated with the commercial license, except for taxes on
      the Project Copyright Holder's net income.

  (d) **Refunds**: fees are non-refundable except as expressly
      stated in the executed commercial agreement or required by
      applicable law.


19. Technical Support

Unless the executed commercial agreement includes a support SLA,
no technical support is provided under the commercial license.
The following defaults apply to any support that IS provided:

  (a) **Support channels**: GitHub private vulnerability reporting
      (security issues), GitHub issue tracker (general bugs), and
      the contact email listed in COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md
      (commercial-only matters).
  (b) **Response targets**: see SECURITY.md for security-related
      targets; commercial-SLA targets (if any) are stated in the
      executed commercial agreement.
  (c) **Scope**: support covers the unmodified, currently
      supported release of the Software running on a supported
      platform (Windows / Linux / macOS as listed in the
      README). Customization, integration, and on-call support
      require a separate engagement.
  (d) **No guarantee**: support does not guarantee that any
      particular bug will be fixed, that any particular feature
      will be added, or that the Software is fit for any
      particular purpose.


20. Breach and Remedies

  (a) **Notification of breach**: if either party becomes aware of
      a material breach of this License by the other party, the
      non-breaching party shall give written notice describing the
      breach with reasonable specificity.

  (b) **Cure period for general breach**: except as provided in
      Section 20(c), the breaching party has thirty (30) days from
      receipt of the written notice to cure the breach to the
      reasonable satisfaction of the non-breaching party.

  (c) **No-cure / immediate termination**: the following are
      material breaches that are NOT subject to the cure period and
      result in immediate termination of all rights granted under
      this License upon written notice:

      (i)  any Commercial Use of the Software without a valid
           commercial license;
      (ii) unauthorized use of any Brand element in commerce;
      (iii) Distribution of modified Core Components under LICENSE
            §3 without making the corresponding source code
            available;
      (iv) any breach of LICENSE §7 (No Patent Grant) initiated
           by patent litigation against the Project Copyright
           Holder or any contributor.

  (d) **Reinstatement after cure**: if the breach is cured within
      the cure period, the non-breaching party may, at its sole
      discretion, reinstate the breaching party's rights under
      this License. Reinstatement is not automatic and may be
      conditioned on the breaching party's written acknowledgement
      of the breach and agreement not to repeat.

  (e) **Cumulative remedies**: termination of this License does
      not waive any other remedy available to the Project
      Copyright Holder at law or in equity, including injunctive
      relief, damages, account of profits, statutory damages
      (where applicable), and the recovery of reasonable legal
      fees and costs.

  (f) **Equitable relief**: the parties acknowledge that damages
      alone may be inadequate to remedy certain breaches (in
      particular, unauthorized Commercial Use of the Brand or
      Distribution of modified Core Components without source
      disclosure). The Project Copyright Holder shall be entitled
      to seek injunctive or other equitable relief without
      requirement of posting a bond, in addition to any other
      remedies.


